        "department": null,
        "description": "This course aims to introduce, through a close reading, fundamental philosophical texts to PhD. Students. The course will involve close readings of influential texts in Moral and Political Philosophy. Topics may include, but are not limited to, metaethics, normative ethics, applied ethics, value theory, moral epistemology, political theory, and political philosophy. It will be held in the seminar format with sections from the text being assigned each week, with presentations by students, followed by discussion. The readings and topics covered in the course will differ across different semester.",
